{
 "id": "socso-act4-2024-10",
 "description": "Act 4 (SOCSO) Third Schedule contribution table with RM6,000 wage ceiling, BEFORE the Non-Employment Injury (SKBBK / LINDUNG 24 Jam) employee share was added. In force for contribution months October 2024 to May 2026 inclusive. Covers financial year 2025 fully and 2026 January-May.",
 "effectiveFrom": "2024-10-01",
 "effectiveTo": "2026-05-31",
 "wageCeiling": 6000,
 "rates": {
  "employmentInjury": {
   "employer": 0.0125,
   "employee": 0
  },
  "invalidity": {
   "employer": 0.005,
   "employee": 0.005
  }
 },
 "lookup": "Band i applies when wageAbove < monthlyWage <= wageUpTo (wageUpTo null = open-ended top band). Band 1 is 'wages up to RM30'. All amounts in RM. Wage ceiling RM6,000: bands 64 and 65 carry identical amounts.",
 "provenance": [
  "Employment-injury and invalidity amounts per band are identical in the pre- and post-June-2026 Third Schedules. Values here are the EI and invalidity columns of Act A1788 Third Schedule Part I/IV, which replaced the schedule but did not change those columns.",
  "Cross-checked: PERKESO Employers' Circular No. 2/2022 Appendix 1 (bands 1-54 identical); Bill D.R. 11/2024 (Employees' Social Security (Amendment) 2024, bands 55-65 identical); PERKESO FAQ on RM6,000 ceiling dated 1 Oct 2024 (top band First Category total RM133.90, Second Category RM74.40); old app table (all 64 rows identical).",
  "Enacted law (deep pass, 2026-11-05): Act A1724, Employees' Social Security (Amendment) Act 2024 (royal assent 11 Sep 2024, gazetted 25 Sep 2024), s.2 sets the RM6,000 limit in s.5(2) and s.3-4 enact items 55-65 of the Third and Fourth Schedules: 0 mismatches against this file. Commencement 1 Oct 2024 per P.U.(B) 381/2024 (listing row only; notice not opened; saved AGC portal listing, unconfirmed: not relied on (D1) until a manual check at lom.agc.gov.my; Circular 3/2024 and the FAQ give the same date). Employers' Circular 3/2024 para 3.3 applies the rates to contributions for the month of October 2024. PERKESO Guidelines 2025 full table: 0 mismatches.",
  "Monthly wages for this table are defined in Third Schedule para 1A (wages payable for all wage periods ending in the month). Para 2 is the A1788 wording, in force only from June 2026."
 ],
